  "claim": "The writer Renascence (poem) of and Robert Penn Warren are both Pulitzer Prize-winners. They both won two prizes for their poetry.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Edna St. Vincent Millay. Sentence: She received the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry in 1923, the third woman to win the award for poetry, and was also known for her feminist activism.\nPage: Robert Penn Warren. Sentence: He received the 1947 Pulitzer Prize for the Novel for his novel \"All the King's Men\" (1946) and the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry in 1958 and 1979.\nPage: Robert Penn Warren. Sentence: He is the only person to have won Pulitzer Prizes for both fiction and poetry.\nPage: Renascence (poem). Sentence: \"Renascence\" (also \"Renasance\") is a 1912 poem by Edna St. Vincent Millay, credited with introducing her to the wider world, and often considered one of her finest poems.",
